U5 cold/warm series for the native and native support families
==============================================================

Same method as the test262 series: a cold arm empties
ZIG_GLOBAL_CACHE_DIR=/data/zig-cache/m5ci-zig-cache-share first, a warm
arm keeps it, and every arm removes the harness object directory while
leaving the runtime archive in place. Linux host, linux-x86_64-gnu.

native-*   = mise run test:native --shard 1/3
support-*  = mise run test:property:extended:native:shard \
               --test-shard=1/12 tests/property/*.property.test.ts

The competing gate on the host finished between native-cold-1 and
native-warm-1, so those two arms' wall times are not comparable; the
second native pair ran at load 1.42 and 1.29 and is. The support pair
was measured once for each arm. Entry counts do not depend on load.

